Figure 2.
The occurence of the Swedish words corresponding to killer slug and super slug respectively.
Those words are
.I mördarsnigel
(pink) and
.I supersnigel
(blue) in 57 corpora in Korp.\**
.FS
The searches covered 57 corpora in the collections
\f[I]Göteborgs-Posten\f[P],
\f[I]Press\f[P],
\f[I]SVT nyheter\f[P],
\f[I]Webbnyheter\f[P],
\f[I]8 Sidor\f[P]
and
\f[I]Dagens Arena\f[P].
.[
Borin Korp
.]
.br
See also https://sprakbanken.se/en/platforms/korp
.FE
Super snail and supersnigel were used in English and Swedish to describe  \f[I]Arion ater \[mu] vulgaris\f[P], i.e.,  the hybrid between European black slug (\f[I]Arion ater\f[P]) and Spanish or Iberian slug (\f[I]Arion vulgaris\f[P]).
Information about the hybrid was first published by.
.[ 
#
Proschwitz 2003
.]
